  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ODI research on UK support for energy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This research is an update of CAFOD&#x2019;s previous research with ODI on UK support for energy 2010-17.  It will review UK ODA support to developing countries for the consumption and production of fossil fuels, to renewables, nuclear, energy efficiency, energy access, and energy infrastructure for the period 2017-19 to determine whether UK support for energy is aligned with the UK&#x2019;s climate and SDG commitments. 
The aims of this research are: 
1)	To understand trends in UK support for energy (focussing on a data set from 2017 to 2019) and establish a baseline to track the direction of travel in the government&#x2019;s international support for the just energy transition.
2)	To support advocacy and build stakeholder understanding on the current scale and balance of UK energy support overseas and to support CAFOD and wider NGO advocacy for a just energy transition towards the UK government and other international actors.</narrative>
  </description>
